  "id": "segregation",
  "term": "segregation",
  "definition": "In this context, segregation refers to a perceptual process in hearing in which an alternating sound pattern is experienced as two distinct auditory streams rather than one mixed sequence. For example, a repeating ABAB pattern may be heard as separate A and B streams.",
